## Scopes

| Scope | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `viewModelScope` | All ViewModel coroutine work |
| `lifecycleScope` + `repeatOnLifecycle` | UI Flow collection |
| `GlobalScope` | **Forbidden** for feature work |

## Dispatchers (mandatory — prevent ANR)

Assume every list/file/query may contain **thousands** of items. Never do heavy work on Main.

| Work | Dispatcher |
|------|------------|
| Disk / DB / SharedPreferences / files | `Dispatchers.IO` in **Repository** (`withContext`) |
| Network | `Dispatchers.IO` |
| Parsing, mapping, filtering, sorting large lists | `Dispatchers.Default` |
| UI collect / state render only | Main (default) |

Rules:
- Inject dispatchers via DI in **Repository** (and ViewModel for heavy `toUi`) — not in DataSource
- DataSource: sync SharedPreferences / thin SDK — no `withContext` on DataSource
- Wrap repository disk/prefs work: `withContext(ioDispatcher) { dataSource.xxx }`
- Wrap heavy mapping: `withContext(defaultDispatcher) { … }` / `flowOn(defaultDispatcher)`
- Heavy mapping belongs in Repository / UseCase; `toUi()` in ViewModel only when needed — never in Fragment/Activity/Adapter
- Mapping domain → UI for large lists must run off Main (`withContext(defaultDispatcher)`)
- DiffUtil / list prep for adapters: off Main before `submitList`
- Never block Main with `runBlocking`, synchronous disk/network, or heavy loops

## Large datasets (design from day one)

- Prefer `ListAdapter` + `DiffUtil` (or AsyncListDiffer) — never `notifyDataSetChanged` for big lists
- DiffCallback: simple `areItemsTheSame` / `areContentsTheSame` as **one-liners** (`Boolean = oldItem.id == newItem.id`) — see `04-mvi-presentation`
- Do not put full thousand-item payloads in State when only a page/window is shown — prefer pagination / paging / windowed loads when the feature needs it
- Avoid copying large collections on Main (`toList()`, deep `map` chains) without a background dispatcher
- Prefer streaming (`Flow`) over loading entire datasets into memory when sources support it
- RecyclerView: `ListAdapter` + DiffUtil; declare `app:layoutManager` / orientation / `spanCount` in XML unless dynamic; avoid nested RecyclerViews that rebind huge children
- Image/list binding: cancel/reuse (e.g. Glide) — no unbounded bitmap work on Main

## Flow

- Cold `Flow` from repositories for continuous observation
- Use operators (`map`, `catch`, `flowOn`) — put `flowOn` before collection so upstream work leaves Main
- Use `stateIn`/`shareIn` only when shared hot streams are needed
- Play Services Tasks: `await()` via coroutines-play-services

## StateFlow

```kotlin
private val _state = MutableStateFlow(FeatureState())
val state: StateFlow<FeatureState> = _state.asStateFlow()
_state.update { it.copy(isLoading = true) }
```

- Private mutable, public immutable — never expose `MutableStateFlow`
- Always provide initial value
- Keep State lean — store display-ready subsets, not raw megabyte dumps

## SharedFlow (effects)

- One-shot events only — not continuous UI state
- Navigation, errors, permission requests

## Exception handling

```kotlin
private val handler = CoroutineExceptionHandler { _, t ->
    viewModelScope.launch { /* map to Effect or state error */ }
}
```

- Never swallow exceptions silently
- Convert failures to Effect or state error flags